  "description": "A complete drape chain: the body model meets every control measure within the avatar tolerance (its ring mesh has torso and leg rings of the measured girths and heights, but no arms: arm length and shoulder width are given by landmarks, and upper-arm, wrist and underbust girths, back width, back length and shoulder length are not represented on it), the physical-simulation scene pins body model, solver, material and avatar profiles and references one draped mesh per panel (same vertices as the rest mesh), the fit map has the avatar profile's zones and is labelled a model estimate, the simulation report carries the configuration's seed, and a general finding on the fit map is allowed because nothing personal is involved. Positions and fit numbers are synthetic."
